<!--
  The words the widgets draw themselves (Kotlin: widgets/WidgetWords.kt), in the
  language the person chose in the app, not the phone's (0.4.43, cb).

  Every word is a pair: name (Bangla, the default) and name_en (English).
  WidgetWords picks one by the home_widget value widget_locale that Dart
  writes (WidgetHub.localeKey): "en" is English, anything else or nothing
  (an app that never ran) is Bangla. There is deliberately no values-en
  folder: Android would pick that by the phone's language, and the widget
  picker and the launcher's own labels would turn English on every English
  phone while the app is still Bangla.

  Dart's words (titles, rows, every figure) come from the ARB files and arrive
  already written inside each widget's JSON; nothing here repeats them.
-->
